          "In broad terms, businesses report outward supplies (sales) and file a summary return with tax payment on a regular cycle, plus an annual return. The details depend on your turnover and registration type, and the official [GST portal](https://www.gst.gov.in/) is the authoritative source for forms and due dates.",
          "Input tax credit is where many businesses quietly lose money. You can usually claim credit only for purchases that your suppliers have correctly reported. Regular reconciliation between your purchase records and supplier filings identifies missing credits early, so you can follow up with suppliers before the deadline passes.",
