          "Weights should be modest and trimmed if extreme. The effective sample size after weighting should be reported, because heavy weighting reduces precision. Weighting can correct imbalances among people who were reached; it cannot correct for groups that were missed entirely. Our [sampling guide](/blog/sampling-and-recruitment-guide) explains how design and weighting work together.",
