          "Payees whose actual tax liability is lower than the TDS that would otherwise be deducted can apply for a certificate authorising a lower or nil deduction rate. When a vendor provides such a certificate, the deductor applies the authorised rate within the certificate’s amount limit and validity period.",
          "Tracking these certificates matters: once the limit is exhausted or the certificate expires, normal rates apply again. Keeping certificate details in the vendor master, with alerts for expiry and limits, avoids short deduction defaults.",
